			"notes": "Beta for Fabric 1.21.1, 1.21.11, 26.2, 26.3, NeoForge 1.21.1, 26.3 and Forge 1.20.1. Requires Xaero's World Map. To see other players' heads, the mod must also be installed on the server.\n\n- Privacy: the server only sends your position if you chose to share it. When you stop sharing, your head disappears at once for other players.\n- Selected sharing: the new \"With\" button shares your position with everyone or only with the players you tick (blue box).\n- Server admins: the game rule `xaeroheadtracker:allow_sharing` turns sharing off for everyone and removes all heads.\n- Heads are cleared when you join another server.\n- Fixed: heads now follow the dimension shown on the map, including with Xaero's dimension button.\n- Fixed: the Fabric 1.21.11 jar is now built for Java 21, and NeoForge shows the right mod version.\n\n**After updating:** if you had explicitly turned sharing on, you keep sharing with everyone. Otherwise your position is shared with nobody until you pick players or choose \"Everyone\" in the settings.\n\n**NeoForge 1.21.1 and Forge 1.20.1, update together:** players and the server must all move to 2.2.0. A 2.1.x client cannot join a 2.2.0 server, and a 2.2.0 client cannot join a 2.1.x server.\n\nBranches that did not have them yet also get the 2.1.1 and 2.1.2 changes: map visible behind the settings, eye button hover and tooltip, settings key on the map, and heads drawn under Xaero's frames (except on Forge 1.20.1).\n\nAlso on [Modrinth](https://modrinth.com/mod/xaero-head-tracker) and [CurseForge](https://www.curseforge.com/projects/1597062)."
		},
